aximum (43.0dBm)\n- **Corrective Action:** Implement gradual power reduction\n- **Configuration Change:** Consider antenna-level power optimization\n- **Risk Mitigation:** Monitor network performance during power reduction\n- **Success Criteria:** Reduce transmission power to meet policy limits\n\n**6. Predicted Maximum Transmission Power**\n- **Violation:** Predicted power (65.0dBm) would exceed maximum (43.0dBm)\n- **Corrective Action:** Implement gradual power reduction\n- **Configuration Change:** Consider antenna-level power optimization\n- **Risk Mitigation:** Monitor network performance during power reduction\n- **Success Criteria:** Ensure predicted power remains below 43.0dBm\n\n**7. Current Autonomous Vehicle Network Slice**\n- **Violation:** Current latency (12.0ms) exceeds maximum (5.0ms)\n- **Corrective Action:** Implement Nokia ultra-low latency algorithms for critical services\n- **Configuration Change:** Enable Nokia ReefShark beamforming optimization\n- **Risk Mitigation:** Monitor throughput degradation during latency optimization\n- **Success Criteria:** Achieve latency below 5.0ms for autonomous vehicle network slice\n\n**8. Predicted Autonomous Vehicle Network Slice**\n- **Violation:** Predicted latency (15.4ms) would exceed maximum (5.0ms)\n- **Corrective Action:** Implement Nokia ultra-low latency algorithms for critical services\n- **Configuration Change:** Enable Nokia ReefShark beamforming optimization\n- **Risk Mitigation:** Monitor throughput degradation during latency optimization\n- **Success Criteria:** Ensure predicted latency stays below 5.0ms for autonomous vehicle network slice\n\n**9. Current URLLC Services General**\n- **Violation:** Current latency (12.0ms) exceeds maximum (1.0ms)\n- **Corrective Action:** Implement Nokia ultra-low latency algorithms for critical services\n- **Configuration Change:** Utilize Nokia energy-aware load balancing\n- **Risk Mitigation:** Monitor throughput degradation during latency optimization\n- **Success Criteria:** Achieve latency below 1.0ms for URLLC services\n\n**10. Predicted URLLC Services General**\n- **Violation:** Predicted latency (15.4ms) would exceed maximum (1.0ms)\n- **Corrective Action:** Implement Nokia ultra-low latency algorithms for critical services\n- **Configuration Change:** Utilize Nokia energy-aware load balancing\n- **Risk Mitigation:** Monitor throughput degradation during latency optimization\n- **Success Criteria:** Ensure predicted latency stays below 1.0ms for URLLC services\n\n**Overall Success Criteria:** Ensure all latency and power parameters are within policy limits, with optimized network performance and compliance with Nokia specific optimizations.\n\nThis detailed healing plan provides a systematic approach to address each critical violation, implement corrective actions, suggest configuration changes, mitigate risks, and define success criteria for each step in a practical manner for a 5G network engineer.",
